{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Betzalel son of Uri, etc., made all that YHWH commanded Moses.</b> Rashi explained: 'which Moses commanded him' is not written, etc. And it appears that Rashi pressed to say this unnecessarily, for in my opinion the meaning of the verse is thus: for we do not find anywhere in all the work of the Mishkan that Moses commanded Betzalel, 'Thus and so shall you do.' For in parashat Ki Tissa it is written (Exodus 31:2), ״רְאֵה קָרָאתִי בְשֵׁם בְּצַלְאֵל״, and it is not written there that Moses conveyed any matter to Betzalel. And likewise in parashat Vayakhel, Moses said to the whole congregation of Israel, ״וְכָל חֲכַם לֵב בָּכֶם יָבֹאוּ וְיַעֲשׂוּ וְגוֹ׳ אֶת־הַמִּשְׁכָּן אֶת־אָהֳלוֹ״ and so forth, and he did not specify there any detail of how the construction of the Mishkan should proceed or in what manner it would be built. And what is said there (Exodus 36:2), ״וַיִּקְרָא מֹשֶׁה אֶל־בְּצַלְאֵל וְגוֹ׳ לְקָרְבָה אֶל הַמְּלָאכָה״ and so forth — there too the manner of their work was not explained, nor how he would arrange them. If so, Moses certainly did not command Betzalel at all how to make the Mishkan and its vessels; rather, Betzalel knew everything through the holy spirit that rested upon him — that which YHWH had commanded Moses. And if so, it was necessary to say here, ״עָשָׂה אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ אֶת־מֹשֶׁה״ — for it could not have said that he made all that Moses commanded him, since Moses had not commanded him the manner of their making." "And as for what Rashi explained, that Moses commanded him to make the vessels first — I do not know whence Rashi learned this, for on the contrary, in parashat Vayakhel Moses mentioned the Mishkan first, and so too in every place the Mishkan is mentioned first, aside from what is said in parashat Terumah, ״וְעָשׂוּ אֲרוֹן עֲצֵי שִׁטִּים״ before the Mishkan, and this is because he is enumerating the order of their rank. And if he learned this from the question, 'which Moses commanded him' is not written, etc. — we have already said that this is no question."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:46.684813415Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}